olithLevel (Anomaly) · difficulty.AllowedToBuild\n    PlaceWorker.IsBuildDesignatorVisible · buildingPrerequisites\n    (ColonistsHaveBuilding) · discoveryPrerequisites\n    (HiddenItemsManager.Hidden) · requireInspectedGravEngine (Odyssey)\n\n`1adc737` amendment #1 named two. Its verification comment #4 corrected that to\nsix and titled itself \"AMENDMENT #1's GATE LIST IS ONE CLAUSE OF SIX\". The real\nnumber is ten, and the three neither comment names —\n`buildingPrerequisites`, `discoveryPrerequisites`, `requireInspectedGravEngine`\n— are the last three. All ten now ship as branchable tokens, so a caller can\ntell \"unresearched\" from \"wrong tech level\" from \"a prerequisite building is\nmissing\" by field rather than by parsing a sentence.\n\nWorth stating plainly since this issue has now been wrong about it twice: a\nclause count in prose goes stale against a DLC boundary. The tokens are the\nanswer; the prose is not.","files":null}]}